  "instruction_steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "instruction": "Preheat oven to 425 degrees. Wash and dry all produce. Dice potatoes into 1/2-inch pieces. Trim, peel, and cut carrots on a diagonal into 1/2-inch-thick pieces. Trim and thinly slice scallions, separating whites from greens; finely chop whites. Peel and finely chop garlic.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abc4d9e6-ab7c-557f-a0d3-9408521cb12c",
        "ddbe0e5c-3f6d-54c4-a469-8778a4420e5f",
        "1115a0ac-3427-582b-89f5-772799e17e9b",
        "2927f331-612f-50cc-b964-679da32e1d1d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "instruction": "In a medium bowl, soak bread with 2 TBSP water (4 TBSP for 4 servings); break up with your hands until pasty. Stir in beef, sriracha, scallion whites, half the garlic, salt (we used 3/4 tsp kosher salt; 11/2 tsp for 4), and pepper. Form into two 1-inch-tall loaves (four loaves for 4). Place on one side of a baking sheet. Toss carrots on empty side of same sheet with a drizzle of oil, salt, and pepper. (For 4, spread meatloaves out across whole sheet and add carrots to a second sheet.) Bake for 20 minutes (we'll glaze the meatloaves then).",
      "timer_seconds": 1200,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "ddbe0e5c-3f6d-54c4-a469-8778a4420e5f",
        "2927f331-612f-50cc-b964-679da32e1d1d",
        "68173350-7942-5115-a8e4-cdb719d14bec",
        "2e84db62-2bcd-5049-9ee9-492adac547a5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "instruction": "Meanwhile, place potatoes in a medium pot with enough salted water to cover by 2 inches. Bring to a boil and cook until very",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abc4d9e6-ab7c-557f-a0d3-9408521cb12c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "instruction": "tender, 12-15 minutes. Reserve 1/2 cup potato cooking liquid, then drain. While potatoes cook, in a small bowl, combine soy sauce, garlic powder, 1/4 cup ketchup (1/2 cup for 4 servings), and 2 tsp sugar (4 tsp for 4).",
      "timer_seconds": 900,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abc4d9e6-ab7c-557f-a0d3-9408521cb12c",
        "2927f331-612f-50cc-b964-679da32e1d1d",
        "608d0240-b08d-54c4-9029-18db46482d78",
        "38de1750-fabb-5178-b207-94a77f59ab0f",
        "73bd315a-14a4-5580-a975-0929ca97fc59"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 5,
      "instruction": "Once meatloaves and carrots have baked 20 minutes, remove from oven. Spoon half the ketchup glaze over meatloaves (save",
      "timer_seconds": 1200,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "ddbe0e5c-3f6d-54c4-a469-8778a4420e5f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 6,
      "instruction": "the rest for serving); return to oven until carrots are browned and tender, meatloaves are cooked through, and glaze is tacky, 4-5 minutes more.",
      "timer_seconds": 300,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "ddbe0e5c-3f6d-54c4-a469-8778a4420e5f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 7,
      "instruction": "Meanwhile, melt 2 TBSP butter (4 TBSP for 4 servings) in pot used for potatoes over medium heat. Add remaining garlic and cook",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abc4d9e6-ab7c-557f-a0d3-9408521cb12c",
        "2927f331-612f-50cc-b964-679da32e1d1d",
        "80df0fd5-7ee5-5e99-be15-71ff8ba378b2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 8,
      "instruction": "until fragrant, 30 seconds. Add potatoes and 1/4 tsp wasabi. Mash, adding splashes of reserved potato cooking liquid as necessary until smooth. Season with salt and pepper. (If you like things spicy, stir in more wasabi!)",
      "timer_seconds": 30,
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abc4d9e6-ab7c-557f-a0d3-9408521cb12c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 9,
      "instruction": "Divide meatloaves, mashed potatoes, and roasted carrots between plates. Sprinkle with scallion greens and serve with remaining ketchup glaze on the side for dipping.",
      "ingredients_used": [
        "abc4d9e6-ab7c-557f-a0d3-9408521cb12c",
        "ddbe0e5c-3f6d-54c4-a469-8778a4420e5f"
      ]
    }
  ],
